WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.240
One hundred years have passed
since the Battle of Galluah Plains,

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.490
where King Kyle defeated
the Dark Lord Angmund.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.910
The Demons rise again,
threatening the world

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.580
and spreading fear and unrest to all.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.660
Demons...

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:34.950
Demons... My mom...

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:40.290
On their way to Ogria Mountain,
Kasel and his companions stop by a shelter.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.910
There, Frey meets a girl named Elise,

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.290
and tries to heal her wounded heart.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:23.910
<i></i>Scars of

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:23.910
<i></i>the Dead

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.240
So is this the town attacked by the Demons?

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.290
It's kind of creepy.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.990
Something's not right.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:47.240
Huh?

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.540
I can't exactly pin it down, but...

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.990
There's something odd...

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:58.990
That person...

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:01.040
Is he a villager?

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.040
I'll go talk to him.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.290
Um, excuse me...

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.660
Roi, did you just...

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:13.870
He's an undead.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:15.330
Undead?

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.990
What is this?!

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.990
Look, there!

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.040
Run!

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:04.410
Don't come near me!

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.200
Wait!

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.830
So this candle must be the light that I saw.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.910
Thanks, um, mister...

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:37.200
My name is Johann. I'm glad you all are safe.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:42.450
They react to loud noises and voices.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:47.120
Please be mindful of that, even while indoors.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.490
What are those people?

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:52.740
And Roi, why...

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.040
Why are there undead here?

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.660
Undead...?

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.080
How long has this been going on?

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:11.580
The nightmare began when
the Demons attacked our village.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:17.910
Several villagers were killed,
but most of them were able to get away.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:22.120
However, a few, including myself,
didn't make it out.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:27.740
We were all afraid of the Demons
and had locked ourselves in our homes.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:34.120
Before long, though, the Demons left,
taking the dead villagers with them.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:41.450
But then, soon after, the villagers
who we thought were dead came back.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.830
What does that mean?

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:50.450
I don't know. We did see them
get attacked by the Demons, but...

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.540
At any rate, we were
glad to see them come back.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:58.080
But those who returned
suddenly started attacking us...

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:01.740
And now, I am the only survivor.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:09.410
When the monsters attacked, I had boarded up
the windows and gathered food.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:13.200
That's how I ended up surviving all by myself.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.290
Viola...

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:19.490
Mom... Liked these...

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:22.370
Elise...

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.410
Elise?!

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.580
Do you know about my daughter?

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.450
Is she... Is she alive?!

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.830
Daughter...?

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:37.240
Yes, Elise is safe! She is in
a shelter in the nearby village.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:45.910
I'm so glad...

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:52.120
We were separated on the day of the attack...

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:56.290
How was she doing?! Was she sad or crying?

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.450
Sh-She's fine...

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:02.740
I'm sure she would be very excited
to know you're alive.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:06.870
Yes, you should go see her right away.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:10.540
I... I can't go, not just yet.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:11.580
Why not?

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:14.410
Being all alone out in a place like this...

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:17.240
I know.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:21.660
But still, I cannot leave this place.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.410
But it's so dangerous!

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:25.490
Leave him alone.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:29.950
He told you he can't leave. Just let him be.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:34.540
By the way, what brings you out to this village?

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:39.490
We're on our way to Ogria Mountain.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:45.540
Ah, I see. In that case,
you should stay here for tonight.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:48.200
It's too dangerous to go out right now.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:53.040
Tomorrow morning, I will take you to
the path to Ogria Mountain.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:57.370
Stay here... with those things around?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.950
They don't care about night or day.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:03.200
In that case, we're better off
moving around during the day.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.830
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.240
That was weirdly tiring.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:10.790
Yes.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:14.700
I get what I felt odd about.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:18.950
For a town that got attacked by Demons,
there weren't any corpses.

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:21.580
Yeah, because they all started moving.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:26.290
I didn't expect to run into the undead here.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:29.830
So what are these "undead" anyway?

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:35.200
He mentioned that the people
who were killed by the Demons came back.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:39.540
Dead people coming back to life?
Is that possible?

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:44.290
The undead are moving corpses.
They never come back to life.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.700
Moving corpses...?

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:51.990
There are instances of dead people
rising up and attacking the living

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:55.450
mentioned in the records of the battle
of Galluah Plains, 100 years ago.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:59.910
It's said that the Demons control the undead.

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:01.330
The Demons...?

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:06.990
Dominix told me something similar,
so I'm pretty sure it's accurate.

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:09.660
But I don't know the details...

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:15.240
Ugh, I should have studied the records
from 100 years ago more.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:18.700
I couldn't because we had to
leave in such a hurry.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:19.870
Sorry...

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:22.540
It's not your fault, Kasel.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:27.080
Dominix needs to stop
making decisions on a whim.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.790
I suppose so.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.740
Roi, how do you know so much
about the undead?

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.490
I also looked it up once,
at the Tower of the Sage.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:41.910
So I guess... those people who are outside...

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:45.160
They all used to be normal humans.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:51.700
Before you get any funny ideas,
no, there is no way to fix them. They're dead.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:57.450
But we can't just let the undead
hang out here. That sounds dangerous.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.990
After all, we were just attacked.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:04.540
You want to go and kill every one of them?

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:08.330
We should concentrate on the Holy Sword.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:10.240
I guess you're right.

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:15.080
That said, I wonder why
that man won't go visit Elise?

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.790
I heard great news today.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:19.540
What do you think it is? It's truly marvelous.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:23.580
Yes, it's true. Elise...

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.580
Elise is alive!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:33.540
I know, Lisa. You're happy, too.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:40.580
But you have to get well first.
This is all I have left, but...

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:45.410
Come on.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:49.240
You have to eat.
Otherwise, how can you go see Elise?

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:55.330
You haven't eaten at all in days.

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:58.240
You won't ever get better until you do.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:17.870
What's wrong?

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:24.620
In the basement...

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:27.290
...there's an undead.

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:28.950
What?

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:30.410
Wait.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:35.160
You have to know how dangerous this is.
We were just attacked.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:40.790
I know. But Mr. Johann seems
to have his reasons, too.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:42.660
What do you mean?

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:48.700
He called her Lisa.
The undead might be his family.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.410
So what?

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:51.660
Huh?

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:55.540
An undead is still an undead.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.540
Let's go have a word with Johann.

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:19.080
Is something wrong, everyone?

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:23.240
You should rest early,
you have a big trip tomorrow.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.580
Hey, what are you thinking?

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:27.790
What is this about?

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:31.160
I hear you have an undead in there.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:35.370
I heard noises, I was concerned, so...

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:43.290
Who is Lisa...?

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:44.950
My wife.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:46.700
Wait, so it's Elise's...?!

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:53.330
I told you earlier about how the villagers
who got killed came back, yes?

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:54.450
Yes...

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:57.330
Lisa was one of them.

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:01.490
So then,

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:06.490
I worked with my friend to capture Lisa!

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:11.540
Capture the undead?! What are you thinking?!

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:14.450
I can't possibly leave her alone.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.290
The undead are just corpses.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:23.290
No! Lisa's still moving!
The dead don't move, do they?!

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:24.740
Dammit.

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.450
Lisa is... unwell.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:32.700
She was hurt by a Demon,
so she's just not herself right now.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:35.580
But something good happened, too.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:39.950
Thanks to you, I know Elise is still alive.

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:43.290
I know Lisa will feel better soon!

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:49.830
You all have traveled all over.
Do you know how to cure Lisa's condition?

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.790
Honored priestess, you must know!

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:03.830
Lisa... Lisa... How do I cure her?

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:08.410
There is no cure. She's dead.
The dead never come back to life.

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:10.660
She is not dead!

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.490
Lisa is alive, she's alive, alive...

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:18.450
Alive, alive, alive, alive...

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:22.540
Do you have any intention of going to Elise...?

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:24.870
I can't leave my wife behind.

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:30.120
I know you already understand,
that there's no more hope for Lisa.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:33.740
You don't know anything about me!

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:37.490
Mr. Johann...

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.290
Please leave us alone!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.740
What about Elise?

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:45.410
What are you going to do about Elise?

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:51.040
Isn't she family, too, like Lisa?

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:52.660
Of course...

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:53.950
Then...

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:57.910
Lisa needs me!

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:06.240
Without me... Without me... Then who...

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:08.240
Who can cure Lisa...?

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:13.200
You want Elise to stay all alone
in an unfamiliar place?!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:15.660
Of course you don't!

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.240
Kasel...

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:25.740
But still... I...

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:29.160
I wasn't able to protect someone dear to me.

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:32.540
She was right there close to me...

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:35.830
No matter how much I wish,
there's no way for me...

00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:38.080
But not you, Mr. Johann!

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:43.540
You can go to her right away!
You can still make it, Mr. Johann!

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:46.580
Please go to Elise.

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:54.990
I know what's right... in my head.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:17:00.620
I know the right thing to do is to go to Elise.

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:09.080
Can you...

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:11.410
...give me a moment alone?

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:21.910
Lisa...

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:25.790
You have to remember, Lisa...

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:28.700
Lisa....

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:33.080
This is the hair ornament
you wore at our wedding.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:40.040
Remember how you always said,

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:43.370
that you're going to give it
to Elise when she gets married?

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.290
Back off, monster!

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:03.450
What did I just...

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:16.660
This should hold her for a while, at least.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.660
The undead have no will, no memories.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:29.200
It looks like her,
but it's not the Lisa you know.

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:33.620
I just wanted to save Lisa...

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:35.660
You can't.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:40.330
The least you can do is to put her to rest.

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:42.740
How...?

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:45.950
Hit it here, to finish it.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:51.080
I can't do something so terrible!

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:53.540
Then I'll do it for you.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:56.200
No! Don't touch Lisa!

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:07.870
This noise...!

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.330
Let's go.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:34.240
These were all villagers...?

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:38.330
If the Demons did this,
I will never forgive them!

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:40.950
Stay sharp!

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:45.330
Why did this happen...?

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:49.660
Lisa... Lisa...

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:52.660
Lisa!

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:58.490
If they keep coming separately like this...

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.870
Cleo! Can't you blow them all up?!

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:08.450
They need to be bunched up more!

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:10.490
Sorry I'm late!

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:21.660
It's not the Lisa I know...

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:26.540
He's right... If you were Lisa,

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:30.740
you'd never forget Elise.

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:43.660
I love you.

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:55.580
I...

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:01.200
...will protect everyone!

00:23:46.740 --> 00:23:51.740
The Guardian Knights decide to investigate
the Galluah Plains for Demons.

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:57.160
Riheet expresses his desire to have
the Black Edge placed in the vanguard.

00:23:57.160 --> 00:23:58.410
He has an agenda on his mind.

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:00.910
<i></i>Individual

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:00.910
<i></i>Motives

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:00.870
He has an agenda on his mind.
